---
import PublicLayout from '../../../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import GuidePdfPreview from '../../../components/guides/GuidePdfPreview.astro';
import GuidePageGallery from '../../../components/guides/GuidePageGallery.astro';
import {agenda,check,jobs,issues,familyPrompt} from '../../../../scripts/lib/weekly-guide-content.mjs';
const pdf='/downloads/family-weekly-reset.pdf';
const images=[1,2,3,4].map(n=>`/images/guides/weekly-guide-page-${n}.webp`);
const art=(name:string)=>`/assets/icons/ofc/guides/weekly/${name}.png`;
---
<PublicLayout title="The Family Weekly Reset: A 15-Minute Plan for the Week" description="Make family schedules, rides, meals and responsibilities easier with a 15-minute weekly reset. Free four-page illustrated Family Weekly Reset PDF and practical steps." width="full" ogType="article">
<div class="omc-guide text-[#545454]">
<section class="px-5 py-9 sm:px-8 sm:py-14"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm font-medium"><a href="/guides" class="underline underline-offset-4">Guides</a><span aria-hidden="true" class="mx-2">/</span>The Family Weekly Reset</nav>
<header class="mx-auto mt-9 max-w-[52rem] text-center">
<p class="eyebrow">FAMILY SCHEDULES · SHARED RESPONSIBILITY</p>
<h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-[clamp(2.4rem,6vw,4.25rem)] leading-[1.09] tracking-tight">Stop starting every Monday already behind.</h1>
<p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-[42rem] text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.8] sm:text-lg">A pickup nobody claimed. A school form due tomorrow. The same dinner question again. Fifteen minutes with the family calendar can take the week's details out of your head and put responsibility where everyone can see it.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-xs text-[#777]">Free practical guide · Four illustrated pages · One 15-minute family check-in</p>
</header>
<div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-8 border-t-[5px] border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6 sm:p-10 md:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr]">
<div><p class="eyebrow">FREE PRINTABLE · FOUR US LETTER PAGES</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl leading-tight">The Family Weekly Reset</h2>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-sm leading-[1.8] sm:text-base">An easy five-step agenda, a family week review, a responsibility handoff worksheet and a five-minute rescue plan for busy weeks.</p>
<ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed"><li>✓ Check the next seven days before they surprise you</li><li>✓ Share rides, dinners and household responsibilities</li><li>✓ Put owners and follow-through on the family calendar</li></ul>
<a href={pdf} download="OMC-Family-Weekly-Reset.pdf" class="btn-primary mt-7">Download the free PDF</a>
<p class="mt-2 text-xs text-[#6f6a65]">Four pages · Email requested on first download · Marketing optional</p></div>
<div class="py-5"><GuidePdfPreview pdf={pdf} images={images} title="The Family Weekly Reset"/></div>
</div>
<nav aria-label="On this page" class="mt-8 border-t border-[#ded8d2] pt-5"><p class="label mb-3 text-[#6f6a65]">IN THIS GUIDE</p>
<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap sm:gap-3"><a class="guide-anchor" href="#agenda">15-minute reset</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#week">Review the week</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#ownership">Share the jobs</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#problems">When plans change</a><a class="guide-anchor max-sm:col-span-2" href="#printable">Free printable</a></div>
</nav>
</div></section>
<section id="agenda" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">01 · A SHORT FAMILY CHECK-IN</p><h2 class="section-heading">Five steps. Fifteen minutes. One shared plan.</h2>
<p class="section-lede">Use the same five-step routine as our existing Family Weekly Reset Builder. A child can join briefly, point to something exciting or name a job. Anyone can lead the questions, while adults handle decisions that need an adult. Choose a regular day that works for you.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
{agenda.map(([icon,title,time,detail],i)=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><img src={art(icon)} width="66" height="66" alt="" loading="lazy" class="size-[66px] object-contain"/><span class="font-serif text-2xl">{time}</span></div><p class="eyebrow mt-3">STEP {i+1}</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-serif text-2xl">{title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}
</div>
<div class="mt-9 border-l-4 border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">This is the logistics check, not a second family meeting.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Keep the reset focused on next week's dates, handoffs, meals and owners. Use the separate Family Meeting for deeper conversations about family goals, connection or values.</p><div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm font-semibold"><a href="/family-meeting-agenda" class="underline underline-offset-4">Family Meeting Agenda</a><a href="/club-2" class="underline underline-offset-4">Explore personalized Club tools</a></div></div>
</div></section>
<section id="week" class="bg-[#D4DFC4]/20 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">02 · A WEEK EVERYONE CAN SEE</p><h2 class="section-heading">Get the details out of your head and onto the calendar.</h2>
<p class="section-lede">Page two is a conversation prompt, not another weekly calendar template. Walk through these five categories and write decisions on the family calendar where they belong.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
{check.map(([icon,title,detail])=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#D4DFC4] bg-white p-6"><img src={art(icon)} width="66" height="66" alt="" loading="lazy" class="mb-3 size-[66px] object-contain"/><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">{title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}
</div>
<div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Dinners and groceries</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Choose Full, Short and Zero nights using the planner you've already got. Don't turn this check-in into an hour of recipe research.</p><a href="/meal-planner" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Free Weekly Dinner Planner</a></div><div class="bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">The family calendar</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Keep schedules, rides, meal plans, groceries and important to-dos in one visible place.</p><a href="/calendar" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Explore the Family Wall Calendar</a></div></div>
</div></section>
<section id="ownership" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">03 · SHARED OWNERSHIP</p><h2 class="section-heading">Don't just list what needs doing. Give it an owner.</h2><p class="section-lede">An owner notices, plans, follows through and handles changes. A list that still depends on Mom to remind everyone hasn't actually shared the work. On page three, write the job, who owns it and when it needs doing.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
{jobs.map(([icon,title,detail])=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#F1D8A8] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-4"><img src={art(icon)} width="58" height="58" alt="" loading="lazy" class="size-[58px] object-contain"/><h3 class="font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3></div><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}
</div>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-6 bg-[#CDDDE1]/35 p-7 sm:p-9 md:grid-cols-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">ASK EVERYONE</p><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl">What would make this week easier?</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Let every family member answer. Then assign one or two concrete changes, not an endless list.</p></div><div><p class="font-serif text-xl leading-[1.5]">“{familyPrompt}”</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Children can choose appropriate jobs. Adults still handle transport, safety, scheduling and other grown-up decisions. A one-adult household doesn't need a pretend second adult to use the system.</p></div></div>
<div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm font-semibold"><a href="/family-responsibility-builder" class="underline underline-offset-4">Family Responsibility Builder</a><a href="/chore-chart" class="underline underline-offset-4">Free Chore Chart Generator</a></div>
</div></section>
<section id="problems" class="bg-[#E8D2D6]/20 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">04 · REAL FAMILY WEEKS</p><h2 class="section-heading">When the weekly reset falls apart.</h2><p class="section-lede">A change of plans doesn't mean starting the process again. Fix the loose end, tell the people affected and update the calendar.</p>
<div class="mt-8 space-y-3">{issues.map(([icon,title,detail])=><article class="grid gap-4 border-l-4 border-[#E8D2D6] bg-white p-5 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.3fr]"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src={art(icon)} width="50" height="50" alt="" loading="lazy" class="size-[50px] shrink-0 object-contain"/><h3 class="font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3></div><p class="text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<div class="mt-8 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">The five-minute rescue reset</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Missed the usual day? Check the dates, rides, the next few dinners and who owns loose ends. Put it on the calendar. Resume your regular rhythm next week.</p></div>
</div></section>
<section id="printable" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">PRINT AND PRACTICE</p><h2 class="section-heading">Four pages to make the week easier.</h2><p class="section-lede">Use the agenda and worksheets to guide your family's check-in. The real week belongs on your shared calendar; deeper conversations belong in your Family Meeting.</p>
<div class="mt-9 border border-[#ded8d2] bg-white p-7 sm:p-9"><GuidePageGallery images={images} title="The Family Weekly Reset"/><div class="mt-8 text-center"><a href={pdf} download="OMC-Family-Weekly-Reset.pdf" class="btn-primary">Download the free PDF</a><p class="mt-2 text-xs">Four US Letter pages · Email requested for first download</p></div></div>
<div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="border-t-4 border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Tailor the 15-minute agenda.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">The Club has a Family Weekly Reset Builder that adjusts the agenda to your household and the concerns you choose.</p><a href="/club-2" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Explore the Organized Family Club</a></div><div class="border-t-4 border-[#D4DFC4] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Keep dinner planning simple.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Use the Family Dinner System to choose go-to meals and share responsibilities.</p><a href="/guides/family-dinner-system/" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Family Dinner System</a></div></div>
<div class="mt-10 bg-[#FBF7F1] p-7"><p class="eyebrow">MORE HELP WITH SHARED RESPONSIBILITY</p><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl">Make the family plan easier to keep.</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-[1.8]">Organized Family Club provides personalized printed family tools and practical guidance. The free weekly reset gets everyone talking; the Club helps your family practice shared responsibility in everyday life.</p><a href="/club-2" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Explore Organized Family Club</a></div>
</div></section></div>
<style>
.omc-guide{font-family:Montserrat,Arial,sans-serif}.omc-guide section[id]{scroll-margin-top:110px}
.omc-guide .eyebrow{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase}
.omc-guide .section-heading{max-width:800px;margin-top:14px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(2rem,4.6vw,3.15rem);line-height:1.16;letter-spacing:-.025em}
.omc-guide .section-lede{max-width:700px;margin-top:16px;font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.8}
.omc-guide .guide-anchor{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:48px;padding:10px 13px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d8d1cb;border-radius:3px;color:#545454;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.25;text-align:center;text-decoration:none}
.omc-guide .guide-anchor:hover{background:#CDDDE1}.omc-guide .guide-anchor:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #545454;outline-offset:2px}
@media(min-width:640px){.omc-guide .guide-anchor{min-height:44px;padding:9px 14px;font-size:13px}}
</style>
</PublicLayout>
